    "solution": "Cross the upper fault deck, jumping and dashing over the two raised piers. Touching it sends one connected crack into the lower seam and under the future anvil chimney. Collect the east tally and drop around the far end. Collect the lower tally, hold Jump during the first downward pod cut for a lofted pogo, and dash left over the furnace cap. Pogo the suspended seed on the far side; continue through the broken seam, take the falling feather and spend its air jump to cross the second furnace cap. On the quiet west floor, down-cut the first anvil into the wide one-way shelf. Rest on the broad shelf, then use the second anvil and a left dash through the missing fault ceiling to return to the now-open entrance gate.",
    "nearestExisting": "F13 changes a later return by spending an earlier surface; F18 uses a changing track and F42 chains deliberate blade launches. This foundry ties those decisions to one connected fault line: the upper road, middle return wall and ceiling above the final anvil are physically the same crack network.",
    "novelty": "The outgoing road is also the obstruction of the route underneath it. Crossing the entire upper deck prepares both the lower wall opening and the final upward return, while actual tallies make the east descent consequential. The lower route changes the movement question from keeping ahead of the crack to chaining a lofted pogo, a suspended refill target and a feather recovery. The ending is the resolved return to the place visible at spawn.",
