    "exit": "The same upper-west overlook after a clockwise circuit of both floors.",
    "interconnection": "Touching the upper fault deck starts the connected crack down through the lower return wall. That same deck is the ceiling above the final anvil; its disappearance permits the return launch. The outbound east tally and lower return tally open the visible gate beside the original entrance.",
    "designNotes": "72×40 tiles (3.13 normal screen areas). The canonical route spans x=-7..560 and upper/lower floors with real horizontal and vertical camera travel. There are no event-proof exits; both tally stones open the normal visible gate. Safe ground beneath the final two anvils allows retries of the ending without death.",
